==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la}} {{term|ingeniosus||endowed with good natural capacity, gifted with genius}} < {{term|ingenium||innate or natural quality, natural capacity, genius}} < {{term|in||in}} + {{term|gignere||to produce}}, OL. {{term|genere}}. Cf. {{etyl|fr}} {{term|ingénieux}}; see also [[engine]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-ingenious.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|iːniəs}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Displaying [[genius]] or [[brilliance]]; tending to [[invent]].
#: ''This fellow is '''ingenious'''; he fixed a problem I didn't even know I had.''
# Characterized by [[genius]]; cleverly done or [[contrived]].
#: ''That is an '''ingenious''' model of the atom.''
# [[witty|Witty]]; [[original]]; [[shrewd]]; [[adroit]]; [[keen]]; [[sagacious]].
#: ''He sent me an '''ingenious''' reply for an email.''

